      {
        "claim": "Scientists identified the source as ice calving from the Antarctic ice sheet.",
        "segment_index": 3,
        "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
        "note": "NOAA described the sound as consistent with non-tectonic cryoseisms originating from glacial movements such as ice calving, with likely sources between Bransfield Strait and the Ross Sea.",
        "correction": null
      },
      {
        "claim": "Seismic cracking events generate massive icequakes matching the Bloop's unique signature.",
        "segment_index": 4,
